layer ddd_fullstack
  use ddd
  use tokio_ddd
  use harness
  use rest_english
  use bus_handle
  use auth_local
  use deploy

  desc "Batteries-included DDD — domain vocabulary + async runtime + HTTP harness + REST routes + auth + deploy hooks. Use plain `ddd` for domain modeling only."
  author "VEIL"

  prompt
    This package uses the full DDD stack:
    - Domain modeling: aggregates, entities, value objects, ports, services, sagas
    - Async runtime: application services are async, domain services are sync
    - HTTP harness: axum server with REST routes, CORS, health check
    - Bus: InProcessBus with Handle-prefix stripping
    - Auth: AllowAllAuth for local development
    - Deploy: pre-deploy hooks

    If you only need domain vocabulary without infrastructure, use `ddd` alone
    and compose your own infrastructure layers.
